{"type":"text","timestamp":1794526698712,"sessionID":"ses_e2de199bcffenOc4bBZXnEEa5a","part":{"id":"prt_1d2204da5002Wmg81Z8qyBtkfc","sessionID":"ses_e2de199bcffenOc4bBZXnEEa5a","messageID":"msg_1d22044900018c9gKtE3JnrcgE","type":"text","text":"T011 is done: only `rankShippedFleet` in `RC` changed, and the verify command passes.\n\n**File written**\n`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs` lines 99-100, exactly two lines:\n\n```js\nhit: shipped.length > 0 && (shipped[0].skillId === hub || shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub),\npresent: shipped.some((r) => r.skillId === hub || r.ownerSkillId === hub),\n```\n\nThe `git diff` for that file shows no other hunk. The tasks.md checkbox is untouched.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs\n[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed\nEXIT=0\n```\n\nThe same command also passed before the edit, so green there alone would not prove the ownerSkillId branch works. I ran a throwaway probe outside the repo against the real function body, with four cases: an `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` leader (hit true, present true), an `ownerSkillId` match behind another leader (hit false, present true), a non-matching owner (hit false, present false), and a plain `skillId` leader (hit true, present true). All four matched, exit 0. The temp directory was removed.\n\n**Could not do**\nNothing. This task does not need the plan, the scratch folder or any build. The new `ownerSkillId` scenarios are T015's job, not this one.\n\nRouting and rule loads: SKILL ROUTING advisor matched `sk-code`. REPO RULES loaded `communication.md`, `communication-handoff.md`, `evidence-and-proof.md`. Gate 3 stayed pre-resolved as instructed.","time":{"start":1794526694821,"end":1794526698712}}}
